+Stages for the 2 h 58 min 20 s video: download, WAV and split about 1 min; transcribe 18 chunks about 6.5 min (slower than the English talk, the audio was Russian); summary about 9 min; compression about 4 min (two `ffmpeg` attempts, 37 then 29 kbps); upload about 1 min. All from the same process samples. The Java bot peaked at 672 MB RSS in this run (186 MB in the 2 h 36 min run), `whisper-server` at 325 MB.
+
+Language: Whisper is forced to English (SPEC: other languages are out of scope). On the Russian audiobook the text came out as a garbled English translation with several repetition loops (for example "I thought it was going to be a new house" repeated about 14 times), even with `-mc 0`. This was not a failure of the bot: the transcript was complete in length (30 855 words for 10 700 s). Use English videos for checks of the transcript.
+
 Peak memory (RSS): `whisper-server` up to 2.1 GB (the model sits in GPU memory, not counted), Java bot 190 MB, `ffmpeg` 62 MB, Ollama about 22 GB for the model (`ollama ps`). Nothing needed tuning: chunk size, `num_ctx` 8192 and `keep_alive` stay as they are, and `qwen3:32b` is fast enough that no fall back to `qwen3:14b` is needed.
 
 Telegram size limit: a file of 51 933 907 bytes (above 50 000 000, below 50 MiB = 52 428 800) was accepted by `sendAudio`, so `LIMIT_BYTES = 50 MiB` holds. The encoder output is about 5% larger than the requested bitrate, so for a 3-hour video the first attempt (37 kbps, about 52.6 MB) lands above the limit and the 29 kbps retry is used; this retry is covered by tests but was not run on a real 3-hour video.
